==============================================================================
=== phase 4: shuffled-donor control (is the content row-specific?)
==============================================================================
  Each row is given the head outputs ANOTHER row's source flag produced, and scored against its own source gold (`own`), the donor's source gold (`donor`), and its base gold (`kept`). If these heads carry the source's identity, `own` must collapse and `donor` must rise. `own` staying high would mean the effect never depended on which image was patched in.
      top-32 shuffled:  own=  3.1% donor= 14.1% kept= 35.9%
      ALL 56 shuffled:  own=  3.1% donor= 14.1% kept= 35.9%   (unshuffled cause was 6.2%)

  -> partial: `own` collapsed to 3.1% but `donor` only reached 14.1%. These heads are necessary carriers of source-specific content but do not reconstruct the donor's answer alone -- report it as 'carries identity', not 'sufficient'.

